  "body": "## This relates to...\n\nFixes #5974\n\n## Rationale\n\nWhen the DNS interceptor has no usable records for a hostname (cold cache, or every cached record has expired), each request starts its own `lookup()`. A burst of concurrent requests to the same host therefore produces a burst of identical lookups; the reproduction in #5974 sees 100 lookups for 100 concurrent requests.\n\n## Changes\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n- `lib/interceptor/dns.js`: `DNSInstance` keeps a per-hostname list of callbacks waiting on an in-flight lookup. Requests that arrive while a lookup for the same hostname is pending join it instead of starting another one. When the lookup completes the records are stored once and each waiting request still runs `pick()` with its own origin (so ports/protocols are preserved and round-robin keeps working). A failed lookup rejects every waiting request and the pending entry is removed, so the next request retries.\n- Requests that pass per-request `dns` options (`opts.dns`) keep their own lookup, since they may resolve differently.\n- `docs/docs/api/Interceptors.md`: one sentence describing the shared in-flight lookup.\n- `test/interceptors/dns.js`: two regression tests — 20 concurrent requests share one lookup and a second batch uses the cache; 5 concurrent requests sharing a failed lookup all reject with `ENOTFOUND`, and the following request performs a fresh lookup.\n\n### Features\n\nN/A\n\n### Breaking Changes and Deprecations\n\nN/A\n\n## Testing (Node.js v22.20.0, Linux)\n\n- `node --test --test-name-pattern='#5974' test/interceptors/dns.js`: 2/2 pass with the fix; both fail on unmodified `main` (20 lookups instead of 1; not all requests rejected by the failed lookup).\n- The standalone script from #5974: `{ coldCacheLookups: 1, warmCacheLookups: 0 }` with the fix, `{ coldCacheLookups: 100, warmCacheLookups: 0 }` on `main`.\n- `node --test test/interceptors/dns.js`: of 37 tests, 33 pass (including the two new ones), 3 are skipped because IPv6 localhost is unavailable here, and 1 fails: `Should respect DNS origin hostname for SNI on TLS`, with `ERR_SSL_SSL/TLS_ALERT_HANDSHAKE_FAILURE`; it fails the same way on unmodified `main`, and leaves the run hanging until my 600 s timeout. I'm relying on CI for that one.\n- `node --test test/interceptors/origin-isolation.js test/interceptors/deduplicate.js`: 73/73 pass.\n- `npx eslint lib/interceptor/dns.js test/interceptors/dns.js`: clean.\n\n## Status\n\n- [x] I have read and agreed to the [Developer's Certificate of Origin][cert]\n- [x] Tested\n- [ ] Benchmarked (**optional**)\n- [x] Documented\n- [x] Review ready\n\nAI assistance was used to help prepare and verify this change.\n\n[cert]: https://github.com/nodejs/undici/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#developers-certificate-of-origin\n",
